! =============================================================================
! Tutorial Problem #3 (manual): Cesium Iodide Scintillator
! =============================================================================
! System: Cs-I. 1 mol Cs, 1 mol I, 1E-5 atm (partial vacuum), 400 C.
! Teaching point: CsI stays solid at 400 C under partial vacuum, even though
! the melting point at atmospheric pressure is much higher -- sublimation
! becomes the limiting process at reduced pressure, not melting.
!
! Note on database: the manual uses an export-controlled CsI.dat; this file
! uses data/CsI-Pham.dat instead, which covers the same Cs-I system from a
! different parameterization, so absolute numbers differ slightly from the
! manual's listing (same physics, different source database).
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/manual/tut03_CsI_scintillator.ti
! Verified output: 1.0000 mol CsI_csi_b2(s), no gas phase stable.
! Sweep temperature (see tut03_sweep variant below, or edit this file) to find
! the sublimation point: with this database, the solid-only -> gas-containing
! transition at 1E-5 atm falls between 550 C and 570 C.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 400
pressure          = 1.0E-5
mass(55)          = 1.0
mass(53)          = 1.0
temperature unit  = C
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/CsI-Pham.dat
print mode        = 2
